        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4 text-base-600">
          <p>
            ABRSM violin preparation lessons with Patricia run 45 to 60 minutes and follow a carefully structured format. Each session begins with bow exercises and open-string work to establish tone quality, followed by the scales and arpeggios required for the current grade. Patricia pays close attention to bow distribution, string crossings, and intonation during this technical work.
          </p>
          <p>
            Repertoire preparation goes beyond learning the notes. Patricia helps students understand the musical character of each piece — phrasing, dynamics, bow strokes, and stylistic context — building the kind of expressive, communicative playing that ABRSM examiners reward. She selects pieces that play to each student's strengths while also developing areas that need attention.
          </p>
          <p>
            Sight-reading and aural training are part of every lesson. For violin students, aural work has particular importance since the instrument demands a well-trained ear for accurate intonation. Patricia also integrates theory discussions naturally — analysing key signatures within the music, identifying intervals, and connecting written concepts to the sounds students are producing on the instrument.
          </p>
        </div>

